# The input, fetched by `make` from github.com/arbace/slim-vim at the commit in
# src/upstream.sha.  Not tracked: this repository records WHICH slim-vim.c it
# was built from (src/upstream.sha, and its digest in src/slim.sha), as
# arbace/slim-vim records the upstream vim commit it was built from and not the
# tree.
/src/slim-vim.c

# The binaries: the input's and the C product's, and the editor's, the core in Go.
/src/slim-vim
/src/whim-vim
/bin/

# The Java and Clojure editors' builds: their sources and classes (make
# bin/braaam, bin/vijure), and the same as one jar at the top (make
# braaam.jar, vijure.jar).
/lib/
/braaam.jar
/vijure.jar

# The Go editor as one go-lisp file (make editor.lgo, doc/GO-LISP.md).
/editor.lgo

# The core half of whim-vim.c, cut at the first #include by `make editor.c`.
editor.c

# The baselines the removed test suite recorded (448e9a8 and before).  Nothing
# reads them any more.
.reference/

# What a sweep compiles, the symbol cache and the binaries' stamps: deleting
# it costs only the time to build again.  (The toolset itself is `go tool
# whim`, cached by Go.)
.cache/

# What a bare `go build ./cmd/whim` would leave at the root.
/whim

# Every temporary goes here, not the shared /tmp: the Makefile exports
# TMPDIR to it, and worktrees go in .tmp/worktrees/.
.tmp/

# Editor swap files: vim names the first .swp and then walks backwards.
*.sw[a-p]

.claude/
